.TH SAY2 1 "2026" "say2 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
say2 \- render Apple's private neural Siri voices from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B say2
[\fISAY\-COMPATIBLE OPTIONS\fR] \fITEXT\fR
.br
.B say2 synthesize
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fITEXT\fR]
.br
.B say2 voices
[\fB\-\-json\fR | \fB\-\-available\fR | \fB\-\-install\fR \fINAME\fR | \fB\-\-purge\fR \fINAME\fR | \fB\-\-status\fR \fINAME\fR | \fB\-\-manage\fR]
.br
.B say2 doctor
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-probe\fR]
.br
.B say2 serve
[\fB\-\-host\fR \fIADDRESS\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fINUMBER\fR] [\fB\-\-engine\fR \fIKIND\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-remote\fR]
.br
.B say2 \-\-explain
\fICODE\fR
.br
.B say2 \-\-exit\-codes
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B say2
reaches Apple's on\-device neural Siri text\-to\-speech voices, which the
public
.BR say (1)
and
.B AVSpeechSynthesizer
APIs cannot select. It writes WAV, CAF, or raw PCM; streams audio; returns
native word timings; and exposes an OpenAI\-compatible local HTTP API via
.BR "say2 serve" .
.PP
It links a private macOS framework and therefore has no compatibility
guarantee across macOS releases. See
.B EXIT STATUS
below for how it reports that, and
.B "say2 doctor"
for a live compatibility probe.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-voice " " \fINAME\fR
Voice display name or asset identifier, matched case\-insensitively.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIPATH\fR
Output file; \fB\-\fR streams raw PCM to standard output. Omit entirely to
play through the default audio device.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-output
Synthesize and discard the audio without writing or playing it \- for
measuring synthesis in isolation. Prefer this to
.B \-o /dev/null
, which fails (see exit 73 below): say2 stages its temp file inside the
output directory for a fast same\-filesystem atomic rename, and
.I /dev
is not a writable directory.
.TP
.BR \-r " " \fIWPM\fR
\fBsay\fR(1)\-compatible words per minute; 175 maps to the native rate multiplier 1.0.
.TP
.BR \-\-engine " " \fIKIND\fR
.BR siri " (default), " av ", or " auto .
.B auto
falls back from Siri to AV on daemon, framework, timeout, or audio
failures, but not on a missing or uninstalled voice.
.PP
Run
.B "say2 synthesize \-\-help"
(or any subcommand with
.BR \-\-help )
for the complete option list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B say2
uses a stable, versioned exit\-code contract so a caller \- human or
automated \- can distinguish a permanent failure from a transient one
without parsing prose.
.BR "say2 \-\-explain " CODE
prints the meaning and remedy for any code below;
.B "say2 \-\-exit\-codes \-\-json"
prints the whole table as machine\-readable JSON. Both read from the same
source as this section, so they cannot drift out of sync with it.
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid invocation \- bad flag, bad value, or two options that conflict.
Will not succeed by retrying unchanged.
.TP
.B 3
No compatible engine could handle the request.
.TP
.B 4
Voice not found \- the name or asset key does not match anything known.
.TP
.B 5
Daemon unreachable: the framework is present but its resident daemon did
not respond in time. Usually transient; retrying is reasonable.
.TP
.B 6
Synthesis produced empty, silent, malformed, or implausibly short audio.
.TP
.B 7
Timed out waiting for a bounded operation (a synthesis render, or a
.B "voices \-\-install \-\-wait"
poll) to complete.
.TP
.B 8
The requested voice exists in Apple's catalog but is not installed.
Recoverable with
.BR "say2 voices \-\-install" .
.TP
.B 69
The private Siri TTS framework itself is not present on this system \-
most likely an Apple macOS update removed or renamed it.
.B This is permanent, not transient.
Do not retry with the same engine; switch to
.B "\-\-engine av"
(or
.BR auto ,
which does this automatically). Set
.B SAY2_FORCE_FRAMEWORK_UNAVAILABLE=1
in the environment to exercise this path deterministically without
waiting for a real macOS update to trigger it.
.TP
.B 70
Unexpected internal failure \- a say2 bug, not a usage or environment
problem. Worth reporting upstream.
.TP
.B 73
Could not write audio to the requested
.B \-o
location \- the directory does not exist, is not writable, or (like
.IR /dev )
is not a normal writable directory.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled (SIGINT/SIGTERM) before completion.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SAY2_FORCE_FRAMEWORK_UNAVAILABLE
When set to
.BR 1 ,
forces exit\-69 behavior unconditionally, regardless of whether the real
framework is actually present. Exists so a caller can test its own
fallback logic deterministically. No effect unless set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR say (1)
.br
Full reference, HTTP API, and Swift SDK documentation:
https://github.com/CaptainCodeAU/say2
.SH BUGS
say2 depends on an undocumented private macOS framework and has no
compatibility guarantee across macOS releases. See exit code 69 above and
.BR "say2 doctor" .
Report issues at https://github.com/CaptainCodeAU/say2/issues .
